From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:56:07 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: moves in from Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Opera, Firefox
 and Safari
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Brave, Edge, Vivaldi and Opera are read as Chrome is (a space per profile,
bookmarks as pinned tabs, open tabs from the session file, history and the
rest, passwords and sign-ins with the browser's own "<Name> Safe Storage"
keychain item); Opera's one profile lives right in its folder. Firefox
(profiles.ini, places.sqlite) and Safari (Bookmarks.plist, History.db) bring
bookmarks and history only, and the step says so; Safari kept private by
macOS (Full Disk Access) says how to allow Meridian. The first run lists
every browser found to pick from; Meridian > Import from Another Browser…,
the command bar and the app menu ("Import from <Browser>…") open the same
step. Tests point each browser at its own folder (--meridian-<kind>-dir).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
